&lt;p&gt;This six-week virtual course hosted by the &lt;a href="https://www.cancer.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Herbert Irving Comprehensive Cancer Center (HICCC)&lt;/a&gt; introduces modern experimental techniques commonly used in biomedical and cancer research. The series provides trainees with a conceptual framework for how laboratory experiments are designed, executed, and interpreted in contemporary research settings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Course topics include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 1:&amp;nbsp;Experimental Design &amp;amp; Research Foundations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 2:&amp;nbsp;Genome Engineering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 3:&amp;nbsp;Cell Models &amp;amp; In Vitro Research&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 4:&amp;nbsp;Immunofluorescence &amp;amp; Flow Cytometry&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 5:&amp;nbsp;High-Throughput Screening &amp;amp; Sequencing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Week 6:&amp;nbsp;Modeling Cancer In Vivo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The course is intended for undergraduates, graduate students, postdoctoral fellows, research technicians, and any trainees who are interested in or beginning laboratory-based research. No&amp;nbsp;prior&amp;nbsp;advanced laboratory experience is&amp;nbsp;required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://cumc.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_etE7XR8XhO3693U" target="_blank"&gt;Register Now!&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join us as we launch the Center for Advanced Diagnostic Research (CADRe)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CADRe is a multidisciplinary center based in the Department of Radiology at the Columbia University Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons. CADRe is dedicated to transforming the way diseases are detected, classified, and monitored. By integrating molecular science, imaging, artificial intelligence, and data analytics, CADRe drives the development of next-generation diagnostic tools and translates discovery into clinical practice, improving outcomes, and shaping the future of healthcare.&amp;nbsp;This event will highlight the depth and breadth of the mission and activities of CADRe and engage the research community at Columbia University, as well as our partners, more broadly into a vibrant scientific ecosystem. We&amp;#39;re excited to have you join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.eventleaf.com/Attendee/Attendee/EventPage?eId=FCQ9a70LIIYQ3pvVw6wttA%3D%3D" target="_blank"&gt;More Information and Registration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Welcome to &lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Crafts &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;on the Corner&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;, an exciting new event series at the &lt;a href="https://theforum.columbia.edu/" target="_blank"&gt;Lee C. Bollinger&amp;nbsp;Forum&lt;/a&gt;. This initiative aims to provide accessible and free opportunities for individuals within the community to explore their artistic potential, enhance their crafting skills, and cultivate a sense of community through shared creative experiences. It&amp;#39;s a celebration of creativity and an opportunity to connect with neighbors in a fun and enriching environment. Open to all ages!&lt;/p&gt;
